From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0010] ir: bounded `for` loops, fully unrolled at compile time

mil_spec::ir was straight-line SSA with no iteration construct. Since the
ANE has no control flow, loops belong at compile time: IR-4 adds bounded
`for i in a..b { ... }` that fully unrolls — each iteration emitted with the
loop var substituted by its concrete value and every defined name suffixed
with `_<iter>` to avoid collisions.

Adds (vendor/mil_spec/src/ir.rs):
- `unroll_loops()` pre-pass on the IR source before compilation.
- `parse_for_loop()` — parses `for i in a..b {` with brace-depth body
  collection (handles nesting by depth).
- `unroll_line()` — substitutes the loop var and suffixes LHS names with
  `_<iter>`.
- Grammar doc line for `for i in 0..N { ... }`.

Tests (tests/ir.rs):
- for_loop_unrolls — N iterations emit N mul ops, output refs last iter.
- for_loop_var_substituted — loop var const substituted per iteration.
- for_loop_empty_range_rejected — empty range is an error.
- for_loop_output_refs_last_iteration — output can name last-iteration value.

Bounds must be integer literals (no variables); only bounded unrolling — no
real control flow, matching the ANE's capabilities.

